\newlabel{tab:lora-per-relation}{{9}{21}{Per-relation DR elimination on SciERC with LoRA fine-tuning (Qwen3-8B). $\kappa $: constraint tightness; $n$: predicted triple count. Used-for gains one triple from Evaluate-for redirection}{table.caption.62}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Four-way constraint ablation on fine-tuned models (LoRA, 2 models $\times $ 2 datasets). DR/RV/ET: violation rates (\%) over predicted relations; CF: over predicted entities; PF: parse failure rate (\%); F1 $\times $100. Grammar layer is a no-op post-fine-tuning (DR change $<$0.2\,pp in all 4 settings; RV and ET already 0\% without constraints). Semantic layer is the sole effective DR defense (41--69\% on SciERC, 2--75\% on DocRED); the near-zero Llama DocRED reduction reflects a near-floor baseline (DR${=}$0.49\%). F1 cost is negligible: max $\Delta $R-F1 = $-$0.30\,pp (Qwen DocRED, full vs.\ unconstrained).}}{21}{table.caption.64}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ft-ablation}{{10}{21}{Four-way constraint ablation on fine-tuned models (LoRA, 2 models $\times $ 2 datasets). DR/RV/ET: violation rates (\%) over predicted relations; CF: over predicted entities; PF: parse failure rate (\%); F1 $\times $100. Grammar layer is a no-op post-fine-tuning (DR change $<$0.2\,pp in all 4 settings; RV and ET already 0\% without constraints). Semantic layer is the sole effective DR defense (41--69\% on SciERC, 2--75\% on DocRED); the near-zero Llama DocRED reduction reflects a near-floor baseline (DR${=}$0.49\%). F1 cost is negligible: max $\Delta $R-F1 = $-$0.30\,pp (Qwen DocRED, full vs.\ unconstrained)}{table.caption.64}{}}
